{
  "case_id": "2004-04-514",
  "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When the Sixth Circuit withdrew its judgment affirming the denial of habeas corpus relief 6 months after this Court denied certiorari review, it exceeded its authority to act under both the rules of appellate procedure and this Court's decision in Calderon v. Thompson."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If you're -- if you're going to -- if you're going to consider something that wasn't a recall of a mandate as if it was, why don't you consider it as a rule 41(b) action?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Rule 41(b) specifically deals with the 7-day period of -- of time for issuance following the expiration of the time for a petition for rehearing or the disposition of that petition for rehearing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Or that a new case has been -- has been released and we think that bears on -- on the outcome."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In our view the rule does not allow any other circumstances. Rule 41 does not allow any other circumstances."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So there -- there is nothing from the court that -- that says we -- we shorten or extend the time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All this record shows, Your Honor, is that the mandate did not issue. So the reason for that is -- is not clear."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Didn't she interview the -- the petitioner herself? Did she not interview the -- the defendant himself?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. SMITH",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "She did."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "At two different points in time, wasn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. SMITH",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It was a deposition. It was attached to a motion to hold the appeal in abeyance pending the disposition of a rule 60 motion in the district court. That's how it came before the -- before the court of appeals."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. SMITH",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It was not properly in the record."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It does not undermine any of the three aggravating circumstances. It does not even make a prima facie showing of insanity under Tennessee law, as I've stated earlier. It simply tracked the mitigating circumstance under the statute, and as this court held in Sawyer v. Whitley, simply additional mitigating circumstances does not rise to the level of innocence of the death penalty."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our understanding is that the Fourth, Fifth, and Sixth Circuits, including the decision below, have all come to the conclusion that the ultimate decision of when to issue the mandate lies within the broad discretion of the court of appeals."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is it that some delays, 6 months, might be really much too late? Is it -- how does it work in the circuits?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What I don't understand is how your argument fits in with -- with the rule that you can't recall the mandate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Shors",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Because this case never became final, as the advisory committee notes made clear -- and we think that the cases that we've cited in the brief are largely undisputed on this point -- a court of appeals decision is not final until it issues its mandate. Even the State in the blue brief concedes that's true."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "District Court",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The district court on February 17th of 2000 had -- had granted the stay."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Did -- did the stay remain in effect in the district court, in your view?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Smith",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State did not need the mandate in order to proceed. A mandate simply directs the district court what to do next. It was not necessary. It is not -- it is completely independent and -- and separate from the disposition of the case on the merits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "but has any judge so ruled in this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In this case did any -- either the court of appeals or the district court terminate the stay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. SMITH",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The stay of execution dissolved upon the disposition of the appeal. The stay was pending the appeal. The appeal in our view was disposed of upon the affirmance of the denial of rehearing. That judgment was final when entered. Finality was suspended only during the timely filed petition for rehearing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. SMITH",
      "case_id": "2004-04-514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "71980649e42dab6a81b31ab164899fb8c80c7f3a9f6f2bf7be75b1c1ef6ee4bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-71980649e42d-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No. There was no formal dissolution of the stay. In our view it dissolved as an -- by operation of law."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
